Vendored ION-DTN private headers
================================

bpP.h is an internal Bundle Protocol header that ION-DTN does NOT install to
its include prefix, yet the CLA sources (mail, mqtt, mysql, quic, tcpv4)
require it.  Verbatim copies are kept here so the contributions can be built
against an *installed* ION without needing an ION source checkout.

Provenance (NASA-JPL ION-DTN, bpv7/library/bpP.h, unmodified):
  bpP-4.1.4.h   tag ion-open-source-4.1.4
  bpP-4.2.0.h   tag ion-open-source-4.2.0

bpP.h itself is a small switch that includes the copy matching the installed
ION: 4.2.0's ion.h defines ION_IPC_ATOMIC_OPAQUE_DEFINED (with the
ion_ipc_atomic_t type), 4.1.4's does not.

The struct layouts these headers declare must match the installed
libbp/libici, or the daemons will misbehave at runtime.  Between 4.1.4 and
4.2.0, BpVdb's delDeltas[] changed from atomic_uint (4 bytes) to
ion_ipc_atomic_t (8 bytes) and VEndpoint gained appCookie, shifting every
field after them (e.g. BpVdb.plans, which tcpv4cla and quiccli read).  When
adding support for a new ION release, add its bpP.h as another copy and
extend the switch rather than editing an existing copy.
